{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"w":0.072595049540201795,"t":"Reading","h":0.014498546631793952,"c":1,"y":0.11295919263629306,"x":0.83508615127122954},{"c":1,"x":0.17691130115534767,"y":0.15381391066591565,"h":0.015522538422134136,"t":"There are also, she adds, a lot of open questions about the ways that ocean debris can lead to","w":0.68939682006835934},{"y":0.17005813940001846,"c":1,"x":0.17695474224506541,"h":0.014570836043610536,"w":0.71399175008138016,"t":"sea-creature death. Many studies have looked at how plastic affects an individual animal, or that"},{"c":1,"t":"animal's tissues or cells, rather than whole populations. And in the lab, scientists often use higher","x":0.17484039632329484,"w":0.72645584106445316,"y":0.18431644584811957,"h":0.017557447453690922},{"y":0.21439471889777872,"t":"fish or sea turtles could die from plastic pollution - or how deaths in one species could affect that","x":0.17686863255189772,"h":0.018203238856806525,"w":0.72447377522786449,"c":1},{"h":0.014534883982160851,"y":0.23255813939789349,"c":1,"x":0.17695473315532353,"t":"animal's predators, or the rest of the ecosystem.","w":0.35596707661946614},{"x":0.17484950297537324,"y":0.26076666117718128,"w":0.70794525146484366,"h":0.018101049677081704,"c":1,"t":"'We need to be asking more ecologically relevant questions,' Rochman says. Usually, scientists"},{"x":0.17687954010710588,"h":0.017432728420298083,"y":0.27598559620229968,"c":1,"w":0.71829188028971336,"t":"don't know exactly how disasters such as a tanker accidentally spilling its whole cargo of oil and"},{"h":0.01675051541996786,"x":0.17687447146800803,"c":1,"t":"polluting huge areas of the ocean will affect the environment until after they've happened. 'We","w":0.70590276082356762,"y":0.29170552207935319},{"h":0.016195524146054074,"t":"don't ask the right questions early enough,' she says. But if ecologists can understand how the","y":0.30800942278068799,"w":0.69958847045898431,"c":1,"x":0.17489712277587349},{"y":0.32259445084222516,"h":0.018481881374183828,"c":1,"x":0.17484684366079761,"t":"slow-moving effect of ocean trash is damaging ecosystems, they might be able to prevent things","w":0.71615376790364582},{"w":0.1512232335408529,"h":0.018536668784205679,"c":1,"x":0.17437611038386766,"t":"from getting worse.","y":0.33985490528495221},{"w":0.72222223917643236,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"x":0.17901233712815079,"y":0.37063953476376255,"t":"Asking the right questions can help policy makers, and the public, figure out where to tocus their"},{"y":0.39780373993688833,"x":0.17475884546433132,"t":"example, the name of theiGreat Pacific Garbage Patch' - a collection of marine debris in the","w":0.6957754516601562,"h":0.021719028306653287,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.41509092604885534,"h":0.016616184944539203,"t":"northern Pacific Ocean - might conjure up a vast, floating trash island. In reality though, much","x":0.17688727525094028,"w":0.7059121704101563},{"h":0.015325941663187237,"t":"of the debris is tiny or below the surface; a person could sail through the area without seeing","y":0.4316262955688992,"c":1,"w":0.68733022054036463,"x":0.17896685847448623},{"x":0.17480953823818973,"y":0.44464829753009427,"h":0.01972992428621223,"c":1,"w":0.71622884114583329,"t":"any trash at all. A Dutch group called 'The Ocean Cleanup' is currently working on plans to put"},{"h":0.015689680798174455,"t":"mechanical devices in the Pacific Garbage Patch and similar areas to suck up plastic. But a recent","y":0.46189384263727318,"w":0.72644948323567704,"x":0.17690809064425991,"c":1},{"t":"paper used simulations to show that strategically positioning the cleanup devices closer to shore","x":0.17689304247164775,"c":1,"w":0.71411799112955721,"y":0.47767499416639136,"h":0.016045606318856986},{"x":0.17901234590285892,"w":0.44238683064778644,"c":1,"y":0.49411071847421206,"t":"would more effectively reduce pollution over the long term.","h":0.013250883392226132},{"x":0.17687177743426977,"c":1,"w":0.63393066406249998,"t":"'I think clearing up some of these misperceptions is really important,' Rochman says.","h":0.019140542325760124,"y":0.52255293669635161},{"y":0.53779082747932938,"x":0.17891901838354726,"c":1,"w":0.68744649251302081,"h":0.01778294200470365,"t":"Among scientists as well as in the media, she says, 'A lot of the images about strandings and"},{"y":0.55370070444265318,"h":0.017539669122235368,"t":"entanglement and all of that cause the perception that plastic debris is killing everything in","w":0.67508677164713538,"c":1,"x":0.17891727339879254},{"t":"the ocean.' Interrogating the existing scientific literature can help ecologists figure out which","w":0.68930043538411456,"x":0.17695472055129546,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"y":0.56976744171264626},{"t":"problems really need addressing, and which ones they'd be better off - like the mussels -","h":0.018172060221749553,"c":1,"y":0.58497496138012195,"w":0.66272857666015628,"x":0.17685301045313528},{"x":0.17695473228038708,"y":0.60306242664593224,"t":"absorbing and ignoring.","w":0.18106995900472003,"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1},{"w":0.024691357612609877,"y":0.86918604634899632,"c":1,"x":0.88271604948587612,"h":0.011627907185728592,"t":"91"}]}